        "# Binary file\n",
        "\n",
        "A binary file is a file object that reads and writes bytes without text encoding or newline translation. Open one with a binary mode such as `open(path, \"rb\")`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-binary-file)"
      ]
